{
  "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
  "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nCAMERON T. NORRIS, ESQUIRE, Arlington, Virginia; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nSETH P. WAXMAN, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent.\nGEN. ELIZABETH B. PRELOGAR, Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Students for Fair Admissions, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NORRIS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nGrutter assumed that universities could use race in a narrowly tailored way if they just did it like Harvard. But this Court never had any evidence about Harvard. Now you do, and that evidence proves that none of Grutter's core assumptions were ever true.\nFirst, Grutter assumed that race would only be a plus. But race is a minus for Asians, a group that continues to face immense racial discrimination in this country. Asians should be getting into Harvard more than whites, but they don't because Harvard gives them significantly lower personal ratings.\nHarvard ranks Asians less likable,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So you agree that, with respect to the essays -- I mean, the Chief Justice suggested that one aspect of racial experience is confronting discrimination. But there are also other aspects of racial experience."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But I guess, you know, in our earlier argument, Justice Kagan pointed out that this gets to be slicing the salami pretty finely."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Norris",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NORRIS: My memory of Fisher II was that the top 10 percent program was extremely successful at increasing the enrollment of underrepresented minorities at Texas. There were other solutions. We -- we have a very sophisticated race-neutral alternative in this case that takes into account socioeconomic status and forces Harvard to eliminate its preferences for the largely white legacies. And that is another way --I mean, our numbers -- the number of -- of Asians would increase on campus; the number of Hispanics would increase on campus; the overall number of underrepresented minorities would increase on campus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Norris",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NORRIS: Black representation would be 10 percent, which is higher than it is in the State of Massachusetts. And that number is -- is quite low. Our expert testified that if Harvard was only willing to consider wealth instead of income, then that number would be quite a bit better because the main disparities we see on the basis of race today is not on parental income but on generational wealth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Harvard -- Harvard argues, though, that we have a compelling interest in diversity writ large and that this Court has deferred to that interest, and among the diverse things that we need to have in our class are children of large donors -- there's evidence about that museum we talked about earlier -- children of legacies, and -- and the squash team. I'm not making it up. It's in the record. And to what extent should this Court be deferring to those interests as part of its compelling interest analysis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF SETH P. WAXMAN ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Waxman, the Petitioner argues that over 80 percent -- that, actually, you could -- you do have available a not -- a race-neutral approach that would yield different but excellent results."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the representation of African Americans, if you just stopped considering race, would go from 14 to 6 percent, but if you also stopped considering ALDCs, it would go to 5 percent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is not considered in any way once the subcommittees and committees meet. It \"fades into the background.\" It is not the basis of admissions decisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0002-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: There was a -- Count I of the complaint was that Harvard was intentionally discriminating against Asian Americans."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: They -- they have a different result because, among the many, many, many characteristics of any particular individual applicant that Harvard considers, one that it does not consider is the academic INDREX. That is, the very metric that they're displaying for you Harvard doesn't even use."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- put aside the hypothetical about the African American applicant who's a legacy. Take two African American applicants in the same category, however you want to take it. They both get or both can get a tip, right, based on their race."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In -- in Bakke, Justice Powell chose Harvard's admission program as a model, and that selection has had an enormous effect for the last 50 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, there are two questions that I want to get to that were asked of you. The first was Justice Alito's about the poor personal rating. It seems to me that Petitioner claims that Harvard's discriminating against Asian Americans because it uses subjective criteria that's affecting the personnel ratings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Harvard",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Harvard greatly values religious diversity. It is extraordinarily proud of the religious --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How can it track it if it doesn't ask about it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 95,
        "start": 95
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "two-thirds of all of the seniors said that their Harvard experience strengthened their ability to relate to people of different races, nations, and religions, and 70 percent said that Harvard's experience had led them to seriously question or rethink their beliefs about a race or ethnic group different than their own."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0004-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A blanket ban on race-conscious admissions would cause racial diversity to plummet at many of our nation's leading educational institutions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0004-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A blanket ban on race-conscious admissions would cause racial diversity to plummet at many of our nation's leading educational institutions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I -- I guess this will be repetitive, but you've said \"true diversity,\" \"meet its diversity goals.\" You know, I'm not sure exactly what that means, and that's -- I'm going to have to figure that out, I guess, but without any more precise guidance on what exactly \"meet its diversity goals\" means as to numbers, it's a little hard to assess, I think."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0005-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: Well, let me try to be more precise. I think that the relevant compelling interest here comes directly from Grutter, where the Court recognized that it is student body diversity in all of its many manifestations. The Court has made clear it's not simple ethnic or racial diversity, and that's what creates a lot of the guardrails in this area in terms of no racial quotas, no automatic awards of points, no separate set-asides or separate admissions tracks. The nature of the interest is not in achieving a precise numerical threshold of minority enrollment at a particular university."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0005-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So -- so a university that -- that did use a -- a -- a numerical goal or did grant a -- a tip based on race alone would be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0005-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: Yes, I think, if a university used a numerical goal and that functioned as an inflexible goal for the university or -- or functioned as a quota system, that's plainly unconstitutional. This Court's precedents don't countenance that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-20-1199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "47499ebb140529313b2a34a93621a62fce283a3cf05e8faadbbc5b73426d01b9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-47499ebb1405-0005-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 112,
        "start": 112
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: General, one of the through lines of the briefs in this case is --I -- I think it's -- it's actually the first line of the Petitioner's brief or something like it -- is -- is essentially Brown compels the overruling of Grutter."
    },
    {
